## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical experience architecting cross-cloud identity solutions, zero-trust controls, and incident readiness for a high-stakes data platform.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-cloud identity federation (IBM Cloud, Coinbase Cloud, Two Sigma)
- STRIDE/PASTA threat modeling methodology
- OAuth2/OIDC token lifecycle management with HSM signing
- Phishing-resistant MFA (FIDO2/WebAuthn, hardware tokens)
- Device attestation and mutual TLS
- RBAC/ABAC hybrid access control model
- Tamper-evident audit trails
- Incident response and testing: tabletop exercises, red-team drills

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo token validation sketch
async function verifyToken(token, publicKey) {
  try {
    const payload = jwt.verify(token, publicKey, {
      algorithms: ['RS256', 'ES256'],
      issuer: 'https://idp.example.com',
      audience: 'data-science-platform'
    });

    // Check token age
    const now = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);
    if (payload.exp - now > 900) { // Max 15 min
      throw new Error('Token lifetime exceeded policy');
    }

    // Verify device attestation claim
    if (!payload.device_trusted) {
      throw new Error('Device not attested');
    }

    return payload;
  } catch (err) {
    throw new AuthenticationError(err.message);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical threat modeling and cross-cloud IAM discipline for edge and cloud architectures—a core CISSP competency for managing distributed fleets and real-time collaboration platforms.

## Key Concepts

- Zero Trust and IAM across edge and cloud environments
- STRIDE/PASTA threat modeling methodologies
- Ephemeral credentials and short-lived tokens (5-15 minute validity)
- On-device attestation using TPM/TEE technologies
- SPIFFE/SPIRE identities and ABAC with OPA policy enforcement
- Centralized KMS/HSM key management with automated rotation
- Incident response tabletop exercises and automation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo token generation outline
async function generateShortLivedToken(identity, scopes, ttlSeconds = 900) {
  const now = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);
  const payload = {
    sub: identity,
    iat: now,
    exp: now + ttlSeconds,
    scope: scopes.join(' '),
    iss: 'video-platform-auth'
  };

  const token = await jwt.sign(payload, await getSigningKey());
  return { token, expires_in: ttlSeconds };
}

async function getSigningKey() {
  const keyId = await rotationService.getCurrentKeyId();
  return rotationService.getKey(keyId);
}
```

